### Exercise 3 — Declarative constraints
#
# Run these with the VS Code REST Client extension (humao.rest-client, already recommended
# for this project): click "Send Request" above any request below. No shell needed — works
# the same on Windows, macOS, and Linux.
#
# The POST requests CHAIN: send requests 1 and 2 first to grab a real agency and customer ID,
# then the create requests reuse them automatically — no hardcoded UUIDs, resilient to the
# sample data this run generated.
#
# `cds watch` must be running in a terminal first.

@host = http://localhost:4004
@auth = alice:

### 1) Grab a real agency ID — SEND FIRST
# @name agency
GET {{host}}/odata/v4/travel/TravelAgencies?$select=ID,name&$top=1
Authorization: Basic {{auth}}

### 2) Grab a real customer ID — SEND SECOND
# @name customer
GET {{host}}/odata/v4/travel/Customers?$select=ID&$top=1
Authorization: Basic {{auth}}

### 3) Create a travel with end date before begin date — rejected with your i18n messages
POST {{host}}/odata/v4/travel/Travels
Authorization: Basic {{auth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "description": "Bad dates",
  "beginDate": "2026-08-10",
  "endDate": "2026-08-01",
  "currency_code": "EUR",
  "agency_ID": "{{agency.response.body.$.value[0].ID}}",
  "customer_ID": "{{customer.response.body.$.value[0].ID}}"
}

### 4) A negative booking fee — rejected with a single, readable message
POST {{host}}/odata/v4/travel/Travels
Authorization: Basic {{auth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "description": "Negative fee",
  "beginDate": "2026-08-01",
  "endDate": "2026-08-10",
  "bookingFee": "-10.00",
  "currency_code": "EUR",
  "agency_ID": "{{agency.response.body.$.value[0].ID}}",
  "customer_ID": "{{customer.response.body.$.value[0].ID}}"
}

### 5) A valid travel — expect HTTP 201 Created
POST {{host}}/odata/v4/travel/Travels
Authorization: Basic {{auth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "description": "Good trip",
  "beginDate": "2026-08-01",
  "endDate": "2026-08-10",
  "currency_code": "EUR",
  "agency_ID": "{{agency.response.body.$.value[0].ID}}",
  "customer_ID": "{{customer.response.body.$.value[0].ID}}"
}
